pinyon-shift-fh1-render-test-v1
# Car physics oracle segment (docs/specs/CAR_PHYSICS.md, SPEC-CAR-PHYSICS):
# free roam on acc9-stock (stock R34) as fh1-physics-accel: wake the car,
# then a straight-line segment with no steering at a fixed 60 Hz clock:
# full throttle from frame 1100 to 1440 (the throttle only takes effect
# near frame 1180; the car is then near 80 km/h, about 55 m on), full
# brake from 1440 to 1700, which stops the car on the asphalt before the
# road bends away (a straight run leaves it near 110 m), then release.
# Holding the brake at a standstill selects reverse. Run with
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_trace=6
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle=true
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_snapshot_frame=1095
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_trace_ticks=800
# and read the 0-100 time with tools/physics-behaviour.py summary; the
# oracle's per-step body trace (physics-oracle.bin, window 0) gives the
# position, speed, gear, loads and slips the spec's reference curves use.
# clock-hz 60
input 0 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 360 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 366 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 480 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 486 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 600 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 606 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 720 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 726 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 780 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
wait 900 3000 vehicle
capture 1090 start
input 1100 0000 0 255 0 0 0 0
input 1440 0000 255 0 0 0 0 0
input 1700 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
capture 1710 end
stop 1720
